Package: lindos-core
Version: 1.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), policykit-1 | polkitd, pkexec, xdg-utils, ca-certificates, curl | wget, gpg
Recommends: xfconf, flatpak, procps, systemd, lindos-tune, efibootmgr, mokutil, libnotify-bin
Suggests: lindos-desktop, lindos-settings, lindos-setup
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos core library, privileged helper and command-line tools
 Lindos is a remaster of Linux Mint XFCE with a Windows-11-style desktop.
 This package ships the pure-Python 'lindos' module (paths, config, modes,
 browsers, hardware, helper client, theme, compat, ram, dualboot, update), the
 polkit-guarded helper /usr/libexec/lindos/lindos-helper, the vendor browser
 installer (Edge/Chrome are downloaded from Microsoft's/Google's apt
 repositories at setup time — their licences forbid shipping them on the ISO;
 Firefox is Mint's .deb), the five mode definitions under
 /usr/share/lindos/modes and the CLIs lindos-mode, lindos-browser,
 lindos-config, lindos-ram, lindos-dualboot and lindos-update, plus the
 read-only lindos-update-notify.sh (login/6-hourly systemd --user timer
 toast when a Lindos component update is available; lindos-desktop ships
 the autostart entry that starts it on login).
 .
 lindos-dualboot restarts the PC once into an existing Windows installation
 (UEFI one-shot boot, or GRUB's one-shot boot on BIOS systems) for games and
 drivers that need a real Windows kernel — never an emulator, spoofer or VM
 trick, and it never edits Windows, BCD or firmware settings.
 .
 lindos-update checks for and applies updates to Lindos's own lindos-*
 packages: from a real signed apt repository once one is configured
 (LINDOS_APT_REPO_URL), or by sideloading local .deb files today. It never
 touches the base system, which Mint's own Update Manager already updates.
 apt/dpkg are always present on a Debian/Ubuntu system (Priority: required/
 important), so no extra Depends are needed for this.
 .
 No GTK dependency: the graphical parts live in lindos-setup / lindos-settings.
